From: Alex Scotti <alexscotti@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] seek: re-arm the BD-J end-of-playlist notification

A seek puts the end of the playlist ahead again, but end_of_playlist stayed
"processed" (3) and is only cleared when a playlist opens, so the next
arrival at the end never sent BDJ_EVENT_END_OF_PLAYLIST. A BD-J menu that
loops its background by seeking back on END_OF_PLAYLIST (Airplane!'s 1s
main-menu clip, 00043.mpls) heard it once and then waited forever on a
black screen with its buttons up. Upstream has the same code.
---
 src/libbluray/bluray.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/src/libbluray/bluray.c	2026-10-07 06:12:01.169431002 +0000
+++ b/src/libbluray/bluray.c	2026-10-07 06:12:01.169431002 +0000
@@ -2001,6 +2001,11 @@
         /* update title position */
         bd->s_pos = (uint64_t)title_pkt * 192;
 
+        /* the end of the playlist is ahead again: re-arm its BD-J
+         * notification, or an application that loops a playlist by seeking
+         * back on END_OF_PLAYLIST hears it only once and waits forever */
+        bd->end_of_playlist = 0;
+
         /* Update PSR_TIME */
         media_time = _update_time_psr_from_stream(bd);
 
